component mc_axis "PLCopen MC Part 1 single-axis state machine with a trapezoid / jerk-limited profile";
author "SyncTwin";
license "GPL";

description
"""
A single axis driven by PLCopen Motion Control Part 1 commands
(MC_Power, MC_MoveAbsolute, MC_MoveRelative, MC_MoveVelocity, MC_Halt,
MC_Stop, MC_Reset, MC_Home, MC_SetPosition) from HAL pins, for axes that
are not interpolated by the G-code trajectory planner: an extra joint of
motion (*joint.N.posthome-cmd*, see *motion*(9),
num_extrajoints), or a drive in a HAL configuration without motion
(positioner, conveyor, pallet handler).  One instance per axis.
*pos-cmd* is the position command, *pos-fb* its feedback.

Compared with *limit3*(9) the axis knows when a move is done, can be
halted, stopped and reset, refuses a target outside the soft limits instead
of clipping it, checks the following error, and reports why it stopped.

STATE CODES (pin *state*, PLCopen axis state diagram): 0 Disabled,
1 Standstill, 2 Homing, 3 DiscreteMotion, 4 ContinuousMotion,
5 SynchronizedMotion, 6 Stopping, 7 ErrorStop.

SYNCHRONIZED MOTION (pins *sync-enable*, *sync-pos*): the axis as a member
of an axes group that interpolates it (PLCopen Part 4, e.g. *mc_group*(9)
in a linear move).  A rising edge of sync-enable in Standstill enters
SynchronizedMotion; every period pos-cmd takes sync-pos (axis frame), refused
into ErrorStop when it is outside the soft limits (5) or one period's step
is over maxv (10): the master plans within the limits, the axis does not
clip.  sync-enable falling leaves it: decelerate at maxa (DiscreteMotion),
then Standstill.  Execute/halt/home/set-position are refused there (2),
MC_Stop stops it.  No command number: the master owns the state.  Not with
drive-profile (the axis stays in Standstill).

BUFFER MODE (pin *buffer-mode*): 0 mcAborting (the only one
implemented), 1 mcBuffered, 2..5 the mcBlending modes.  Anything but 0 is refused
with error-id 1.

MOVE MODE (pin *mode*): 0 absolute (MC_MoveAbsolute), 1 relative
(MC_MoveRelative), 2 velocity (MC_MoveVelocity, direction = sign of
*velocity*).

MC_SETPOSITION (pin *set-position*): a rising edge in Standstill makes
*position* the axis's actual position (mode 1: actual + position), no
motion; Done in the same period.  The shift is an offset of the axis
(axis position = pos-fb + offset): pos-cmd and pos-fb stay in the drive's
frame, so the drive sees no step.  The absolute target, the soft limits and
actual-position are in the axis frame.  In any other state it is refused
(error 2).  MC_Home clears the offset; so does reloading the component.

ERROR IDS (pin *error-id*): 1 buffer mode not implemented, 2 command
not allowed in this state, 3 drive fault, 4 following error over ferror-max,
5 soft limit (target outside, or reached in velocity mode), 6 drive left
operation-enabled while powered, 7 invalid limits/parameters (maxv, maxa,
ferror-max must be > 0, max-limit > min-limit), 8 unknown mode, 9 homing
error (statusword bit 13 while the drive homes), 10 synchronized step over
maxv.

ONE MULTIPLEXED FB: one set of outputs per axis, not one per function block
instance.  The outputs belong to the NEWEST command or event, so that Busy,
Done, Error and CommandAborted are mutually exclusive in every period
(PLCopen Part 1, 2.4.1): a refused command takes Error over a move that
keeps running (it drops Busy/Active, and the move's own completion raises no
Done); an axis error takes Error over the command it ended.
*error-id* is that newest outcome: the refusal code, else the
ErrorStop reason.  *axis-error-id* is the axis alone
(MC_ReadAxisError): why the axis is in ErrorStop, 0 outside it.  Done,
CommandAborted and a refusal Error stay while the input that started the
command (execute/halt/stop/reset/home/set-position) is held and are reset
one period after it falls; the ErrorStop reason stays until MC_Reset.

COMMAND NUMBERS (pins *command-id*, *done-id*,
*aborted-id*, *failed-id*): every rising edge of
execute/halt/stop/reset/home/set-position gets the next number on
command-id; the axis resolves each command by its number: done-id when it
completed, aborted-id when another command or power-off ended it,
failed-id when it was refused or an axis error ended it.  This lets one
axis serve several callers: a caller keeps the number command-id showed
after its own edge and is Busy until that number appears on done-id,
aborted-id or failed-id.

MC_HOME (pin *home*): the drive homes itself (CiA-402 homing mode,
e.g. the cia402 component of linuxcnc-ethercat).  Homing is armed once
stat-homed reads 0 (a stale 1 from an earlier homing is not taken for
success) and ends on the next 1; the axis clears drive-home itself.  Bit 13
of drv-statusword while armed is a homing error (ErrorStop 9).  An extra
joint of motion is homed by motion instead: wire joint.N.homed to
stat-op-enabled and leave home unconnected.

DRIVE PROFILE (pin *drive-profile* = 1): for a drive without cyclic
position mode (CiA-402 Profile Position).  An accepted absolute/relative
move is handed over whole: pos-cmd = target, move-velocity,
move-acceleration, one period of move-execute; done comes from
drv-move-done (seen 0 after the set-point, then 1).  Halt/stop and ErrorStop
raise move-halt.  No own profile, no following-error check (the drive
checks it).  Velocity moves are refused (error 8).  With drive-profile = 0
(default) none of this runs.

ACCELERATION, DECELERATION, JERK (inputs of MC_Move*): *acceleration*
raises |v| (0 = the axis default maxa), *deceleration* lowers it
(0 = same as acceleration), both capped by maxa.  *jerk* = 0 is no
jerk limit (trapezoid); jerk > 0 is a jerk-limited S-curve, implemented for
velocity moves (MC_MoveVelocity and MC_Halt of such a move).  A position
move with jerk > 0 is refused (error 7), not ignored; so is drive-profile
with a jerk or a deceleration different from acceleration.  MC_Stop and
ErrorStop brake at maxa without a jerk limit.

CONTINUOUS AXIS (pin *limits-enable* = 0): a modulo axis without soft
limits; min-limit/max-limit are not checked, a velocity move runs until
halt/stop; maxv, maxa and ferror-max stay in force.

Transitions follow the PLCopen state diagram: motion only from Standstill
or a motion state; ErrorStop is left only through reset; Stopping holds
while stop is 1.  The following-error check is always on while powered; a
non-positive ferror-max keeps the axis Disabled (error 7) instead of
disabling the check.

AXIS READINGS (MC_ReadActualPosition, MC_ReadActualTorque,
MC_ReadActualVelocity): a caller reads them at the axis, never at the bus:
*actual-position* (pos-fb plus the MC_SetPosition offset), *torque-fb* (per
mille of rated torque, as the drive reports object 0x6077), *velocity-fb*
(machine units/s) and *statusword* (object 0x6041 as is).  They are fed by
the raw inputs drv-torque, drv-velocity and drv-statusword.
""";

notes
"""
Wiring to an extra joint of motion (see configs/sim/axis/extrajoints/mc_axis.ini):

----
net ax-cmd  ax4.pos-cmd    => joint.4.posthome-cmd
net ax-fb   joint.4.pos-fb => ax4.pos-fb
net ax-ok   joint.4.homed  => ax4.stat-op-enabled
setp ax4.maxv [JOINT_4]MAX_VELOCITY  (and maxa, min-limit, max-limit, ferror-max)
----

Wiring to a CiA-402 drive (cia402 component of linuxcnc-ethercat, per axis N):

----
net ax-cmd   mc-axis.N.pos-cmd         => cia402.N.pos-cmd
net ax-fb    cia402.N.pos-fb           => mc-axis.N.pos-fb
net ax-en    mc-axis.N.enable-out      => cia402.N.enable
net ax-opena cia402.N.stat-op-enabled  => mc-axis.N.stat-op-enabled
net ax-flt   cia402.N.drv-fault        => mc-axis.N.drv-fault
net ax-frst  mc-axis.N.fault-reset-out => cia402.N.fault-reset
net ax-homd  cia402.N.stat-homed       => mc-axis.N.stat-homed
net ax-home  mc-axis.N.drive-home     <=> cia402.N.home
net ax-vel   cia402.N.velocity-fb      => mc-axis.N.drv-velocity
net ax-trq   <0x6077 PDO pin>          => mc-axis.N.drv-torque
net ax-sw    <0x6041 PDO pin>          => mc-axis.N.drv-statusword
----

The target (position, mode, velocity) must be computed no later than the
execute edge in the same thread.

Tested on a CiA-402 EtherCAT servo (Inovance SV660N, cyclic synchronous
position) and on the extrajoints sim.
""";

// ---- commands (PLCopen FB inputs, one set per axis)
pin in bool power "MC_Power.Enable";
pin in bool execute "rising edge starts the move described by mode/position/velocity/acceleration";
pin in bool halt "rising edge: MC_Halt: decelerate to standstill, stays interruptible";
pin in bool stop "MC_Stop: rising edge enters Stopping (Busy), Done at standstill while stop is 1, Standstill on release";
pin in bool reset "rising edge: MC_Reset: leave ErrorStop (also drives fault-reset-out)";
pin in bool home "rising edge: MC_Home through the drive's own homing (cia402.home)";
pin in bool set_position "rising edge: MC_SetPosition: position (mode 1: relative) becomes the actual position, no motion; Standstill only";
pin in real position "target (absolute) or distance (relative), machine units";
pin in real velocity "velocity limit of the move; in velocity mode the signed target velocity";
pin in real acceleration "acceleration of the move (|v| rising), capped by maxa; 0 = maxa (axis default)";
pin in real deceleration "deceleration of the move (|v| falling), capped by maxa; 0 = acceleration";
pin in real jerk "jerk limit of the move; 0 = none (trapezoid), > 0 = S-curve (velocity moves only)";
pin in sint mode "0 absolute, 1 relative, 2 velocity (set-position: 0 absolute, 1 relative)";
pin in sint buffer_mode "index in BUFFER_MODES; only 0 (mcAborting) implemented";
pin in bool sync_enable "rising edge in Standstill: SynchronizedMotion, pos-cmd follows sync-pos (axes group master)";
pin in real sync_pos "SynchronizedMotion: the position the master gives this period (axis frame)";

// ---- limits, as in [JOINT_n] of a machine config
pin in real min_limit "soft limit low, [JOINT_n]MIN_LIMIT";
pin in real max_limit "soft limit high, [JOINT_n]MAX_LIMIT";
pin in bool limits_enable = 1 "0: continuous (modulo) joint without soft limits: min/max ignored, maxv/maxa/ferror-max still apply";
pin in real maxv "velocity ceiling, [JOINT_n]MAX_VELOCITY";
pin in real maxa "acceleration ceiling, [JOINT_n]MAX_ACCELERATION";
pin in real ferror_max "following error that trips ErrorStop, [JOINT_n]FERROR";

// ---- from the drive (e.g. cia402)
pin in bool stat_op_enabled "cia402.N.stat-op-enabled";
pin in bool drv_fault "cia402.N.drv-fault";
pin in bool stat_homed "cia402.N.stat-homed";
pin in real pos_fb "cia402.N.pos-fb";
pin in sint drv_torque "drive actual torque 0x6077 (per mille of rated), raw from the bus";
pin in real drv_velocity "cia402.N.velocity-fb (machine units/s)";
pin in uint drv_statusword "drive statusword 0x6041, raw from the bus";
pin in uint drive_error "drive error code 0x603F as read, 0 = no fault (passed through for the caller, not interpreted)";

// ---- to the drive (e.g. cia402)
pin out real pos_cmd "to cia402.N.pos-cmd";
pin out real vel_cmd "commanded velocity of the profile (for display/feed-forward)";
pin out bool enable_out "to cia402.N.enable";
pin out bool fault_reset_out "to cia402.N.fault-reset, high while a reset is pending in ErrorStop";
pin io bool drive_home "to cia402.N.home (io: cia402 clears it when the drive has homed)";

// ---- drive profile: only with drive-profile = 1, inert otherwise
pin in bool drive_profile = 0 "1: the drive plans the move (CiA-402 PP, cia402 pp-mode): no own trapezoid, pos-cmd is the target, the drive's 0x6065 guards the following error";
pin in bool drv_move_done "cia402.N.pp-done";
pin out bool move_execute "to cia402.N.pp-execute: one period high per accepted move";
pin out bool move_halt "to cia402.N.pp-halt: high while halting/stopping";
pin out real move_velocity "to cia402.N.pp-velocity";
pin out real move_acceleration "to cia402.N.pp-accel";

// ---- status (PLCopen FB outputs)
pin out sint state "AxisState code";
pin out bool busy;
pin out bool done;
pin out bool active;
pin out bool command_aborted;
pin out bool in_velocity "velocity mode reached its target velocity";
pin out bool error;
pin out sint error_id "outcome of the newest command: refusal code, else the ErrorStop reason";
pin out sint axis_error_id "MC_ReadAxisError: why the axis is in ErrorStop, 0 outside it";
pin out uint command_id "number of the newest command (rising edge of execute/halt/stop/reset/home); busy/done/error/command-aborted/error-id belong to it";
pin out uint done_id "number of the last command that completed (Done)";
pin out uint aborted_id "number of the last command aborted by another command or by power-off (CommandAborted)";
pin out uint failed_id "number of the last command refused or ended by an axis error (Error)";
pin out real ferror "pos-cmd minus pos-fb";
pin out real actual_position "MC_ReadActualPosition: pos-fb + the MC_SetPosition offset (axis frame)";
pin out real torque_fb "MC_ReadActualTorque: per mille of rated torque";
pin out real velocity_fb "MC_ReadActualVelocity: machine units/s";
pin out uint statusword "drive statusword 0x6041 as read";

variable double v;          // profile velocity
variable double tgt;        // position target of the running move
variable double cmd_vel;    // velocity cap / target of the running move
variable double cmd_acc;    // acceleration of the running move
variable double cmd_dec;    // deceleration of the running move
variable double cmd_jerk;   // jerk limit of the running move, 0 = trapezoid
variable double a_cur;      // profile acceleration (continuity for the S-curve)
variable int run;           // 0 none, 1 position move, 2 velocity move, 3 decel-to-stop
variable int err_latched;   // axis error (ErrorStop) id
variable int cmd_err;       // command refusal id (does not change state)
variable int reset_req;
variable int term_shown;  // a terminal output (done/aborted/refusal) has been out one period
variable int seq;         // last command number given out (command-id)
variable int run_id;      // number of the command the axis is executing, 0 none
variable int owner;       // input of the newest command: 1 execute 2 halt 3 stop 4 reset 5 home 6 set-position, 0 none
variable int execute_old;
variable int halt_old;
variable int stop_old;
variable int reset_old;
variable int home_old;
variable int set_old;
variable int sync_old;
variable double off;        // MC_SetPosition offset: axis position = drive position (pos-fb) + off
variable int home_started;  // homing armed: stat-homed seen 0 since the request
variable int move_armed;    // drive-profile: drv-move-done seen 0 since the set-point (a halt keeps it:
                            // done already 1 at the halt means the drive stands)

function _;
;;

#include <rtapi_math.h>

/* pin state: PLCopen axis states */
#define ST_DISABLED 0
#define ST_STANDSTILL 1
#define ST_HOMING 2
#define ST_DISCRETE_MOTION 3
#define ST_CONTINUOUS_MOTION 4
#define ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION 5
#define ST_STOPPING 6
#define ST_ERROR_STOP 7

/* pin error-id */
#define E_BUFFER_MODE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED 1
#define E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE 2
#define E_DRIVE_FAULT 3
#define E_FOLLOWING_ERROR_OVER_LIMIT 4
#define E_SOFT_LIMIT 5
#define E_DRIVE_LEFT_OPERATION_ENABLED 6
#define E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS 7
#define E_UNKNOWN_MODE 8
#define E_HOMING_ERROR 9
#define E_SYNC_STEP_OVER_MAXV 10

#define RUN_NONE 0
#define RUN_POS  1
#define RUN_VEL  2
#define RUN_STOP 3

static int limits_ok(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    return maxv > 0.0 && maxa > 0.0 && ferror_max > 0.0
        && (!limits_enable || max_limit > min_limit);
}

/* Set the ramps of a stop at the axis ceiling: trapezoid, no jerk limit. */
static void ramps_max(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    cmd_acc = cmd_dec = maxa > 0.0 ? maxa : 1e9;  /* no valid ceiling: stop at once */
    cmd_jerk = 0.0;
}

/* One period of the jerk-limited velocity ramp toward vreq (S-curve): the
 * position trapezoid below one derivative up: the acceleration that still
 * rounds off to 0 exactly at vreq at jerk J (a^2 = 2 J dv, corrected by one
 * period), capped by cmd_acc while |v| rises and cmd_dec while it falls,
 * reached at rate J. */
static void scurve_step(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, double vreq, double dt) {
    double rem = vreq - v, dj = cmd_jerk * dt, alim, areq;
    if (fabs(rem) <= 0.5 * dj * dt && fabs(a_cur) <= dj) { v = vreq; a_cur = 0.0; return; }
    alim = (v == 0.0 || (v > 0.0) == (rem > 0.0)) ? cmd_acc : cmd_dec;
    areq = -dj + sqrt(2.0 * cmd_jerk * fabs(rem) + dj * dj);
    if (areq > alim) areq = alim;
    if (rem < 0.0) areq = -areq;
    if (areq > a_cur + dj) a_cur += dj;
    else if (areq < a_cur - dj) a_cur -= dj;
    else a_cur = areq;
    v += a_cur * dt;
}

/* One period of the profile.  Position move: the velocity that still stops
 * exactly at the target with deceleration cmd_dec (v^2 = 2 d s, corrected by one
 * period of discretisation), capped by vcap; |v| rises at cmd_acc and falls at
 * cmd_dec (trapezoid).  Velocity move / stop: ramp to vcap (signed) or 0, an
 * S-curve when cmd_jerk > 0.  Returns 1 when the move is finished. */
static int profile_step(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, double dt) {
    double dd = cmd_dec * dt, vreq, vold = v, d, r;
    int fin = 0;
    if (run == RUN_POS) {
        d = tgt - pos_cmd;
        if (fabs(d) <= 0.5 * dd * dt && fabs(v) <= dd) {
            pos_cmd_set(tgt); v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0;
            return 1;
        }
        vreq = -dd + sqrt(2.0 * cmd_dec * fabs(d) + dd * dd);
        /* a velocity move that turned into the stop at its soft limit keeps its
         * signed cmd_vel: cap by the magnitude, the sign comes from d below */
        if (vreq > fabs(cmd_vel)) vreq = fabs(cmd_vel);
        if (d < 0) vreq = -vreq;
    } else if (run == RUN_VEL) {
        vreq = cmd_vel;
    } else {
        vreq = 0.0;
    }
    if (cmd_jerk > 0.0 && run != RUN_POS) {
        scurve_step(__comp_inst, vreq, dt);
    } else {
        /* |v| falls toward vreq: deceleration, else acceleration */
        r = ((v > 0.0 && vreq < v) || (v < 0.0 && vreq > v)) ? cmd_dec : cmd_acc;
        r *= dt;
        if (vreq > v + r) v += r;
        else if (vreq < v - r) v -= r;
        else v = vreq;
        a_cur = v == vreq ? 0.0 : (v - vold) / dt;
    }
    pos_cmd_set(pos_cmd + (0.5 * (v + vold) * dt));
    if (run == RUN_STOP && v == 0.0 && a_cur == 0.0) fin = 1;
    if (run == RUN_VEL) in_velocity_set((v == cmd_vel));
    return fin;
}

static void end_command(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int aborted) {
    if (busy && aborted) { command_aborted_set(1); term_shown = 0; }
    if (run_id) {   /* the command is resolved by number even when newer ones own the outputs */
        if (aborted) aborted_id_set(run_id); else done_id_set(run_id);
        run_id = 0;
    }
    busy_set(0); active_set(0); in_velocity_set(0);
}

/* A command finished: Done only when it still owns the outputs (busy) -
 * a newer, refused command keeps them (PLCopen Part 1, 2.4.1). */
static void complete(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    int mine = busy;
    end_command(__comp_inst, 0);
    if (mine) { done_set(1); term_shown = 0; }
}

static void to_errorstop(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int id) {
    if (state == ST_ERROR_STOP) return;
    if (drive_profile) move_halt_set(1);
    err_latched = id;
    cmd_err = 0;   /* the axis error is the newest event: it owns error-id */
    if (run_id) { failed_id_set(run_id); run_id = 0; }
    end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
    state_set(ST_ERROR_STOP);
    run = RUN_STOP;
    ramps_max(__comp_inst);
}

/* Accept a move command; returns 0 and sets cmd_err when refused. */
static int accept_move(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    double t, lo = min_limit - off, hi = max_limit - off;   /* soft limits in the drive frame */
    if (buffer_mode != 0) { cmd_err = E_BUFFER_MODE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED; return 0; }
    if (mode < 0 || mode > 2) { cmd_err = E_UNKNOWN_MODE; return 0; }
    double acc = acceleration > 0.0 && acceleration < maxa ? acceleration : maxa;   /* 0 = axis default */
    if (acceleration < 0.0 || maxa <= 0.0 || deceleration < 0.0 || jerk < 0.0) {
        cmd_err = E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS; return 0;
    }
    /* drive-profile: velocity moves need PV, not implemented yet */
    if (drive_profile && mode == 2) { cmd_err = E_UNKNOWN_MODE; return 0; }
    /* refused, not ignored: the S-curve is a velocity-move ramp; pp has one ramp */
    if (jerk > 0.0 && (mode != 2 || drive_profile)) { cmd_err = E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS; return 0; }
    if (drive_profile && deceleration > 0.0 && deceleration != acc) {
        cmd_err = E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS; return 0;
    }
    cmd_acc = acc;
    cmd_dec = deceleration > 0.0 ? (deceleration < maxa ? deceleration : maxa) : cmd_acc;
    cmd_jerk = jerk;
    if (mode == 2) {
        t = velocity;
        if (t > maxv) t = maxv;
        if (t < -maxv) t = -maxv;
        if (limits_enable && ((t > 0.0 && pos_cmd >= hi) || (t < 0.0 && pos_cmd <= lo))) {
            cmd_err = E_SOFT_LIMIT; return 0;
        }
        cmd_vel = t;
        /* soft limits bound a velocity move: it plans toward the limit it heads to */
        tgt = t >= 0.0 ? hi : lo;
        run = RUN_VEL;
        state_set(ST_CONTINUOUS_MOTION);
    } else {
        if (velocity <= 0.0) { cmd_err = E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS; return 0; }
        t = (mode == 0) ? position - off : pos_cmd + position;
        if (limits_enable && (t < lo || t > hi)) { cmd_err = E_SOFT_LIMIT; return 0; }
        tgt = t;
        cmd_vel = velocity < maxv ? velocity : maxv;
        run = RUN_POS;
        state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION);
        if (drive_profile) {
            /* hand the whole move to the drive: target, velocity, acceleration */
            pos_cmd_set(tgt);
            move_velocity_set(cmd_vel);
            move_acceleration_set(cmd_acc);
            move_halt_set(0);
            move_execute_set(1);
            move_armed = 0;
        }
    }
    return 1;
}

FUNCTION(_) {
    double dt = period * 1e-9;
    int ex_edge = execute && !execute_old;
    int halt_edge = halt && !halt_old;
    int stop_edge = stop && !stop_old;
    int reset_edge = reset && !reset_old;
    int home_edge = home && !home_old;
    int set_edge = set_position && !set_old;
    int sync_edge = sync_enable && !sync_old;
    int cfg = limits_ok(__comp_inst);
    execute_old = execute; halt_old = halt; stop_old = stop;
    reset_old = reset; home_old = home; set_old = set_position; sync_old = sync_enable;
    if (drive_profile) move_execute_set(0);   /* a set-point is one period long */

    /* PLCopen Part 1, 2.4.1: Done, CommandAborted and a command's Error stay while the
     * input that started the command is held, and at least one period after
     * it falls; then they are reset.  The axis error (ErrorStop reason) is
     * not a command's output: it stays until MC_Reset. */
    {
        int held = (owner == 1 && execute) || (owner == 2 && halt) || (owner == 3 && stop)
                || (owner == 4 && reset) || (owner == 5 && home) || (owner == 6 && set_position);
        if (done || command_aborted || cmd_err) {
            if (term_shown && !held) { done_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); cmd_err = 0; }
            term_shown = 1;
        }
    }
    if (ex_edge || halt_edge || home_edge || reset_edge || stop_edge || set_edge) {
        cmd_err = 0; command_aborted_set(0); done_set(0); term_shown = 0;
        owner = stop_edge ? 3 : ex_edge ? 1 : halt_edge ? 2 : home_edge ? 5 : set_edge ? 6 : 4;
        seq = seq == 0x7fffffff ? 1 : seq + 1;   /* 0 = no command */
        command_id_set(seq);
    }

    enable_out_set(power && cfg);

    /* ---- transitions valid from any state (PLCopen diagram) */
    if (drv_fault && state != ST_DISABLED) {
        to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_DRIVE_FAULT);
    } else if (drv_fault && power) {
        to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_DRIVE_FAULT);
    }
    if (!power && state != ST_ERROR_STOP && state != ST_DISABLED) {
        end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
        drive_home_set(0);   /* a pending home request must not survive power-off */
        state_set(ST_DISABLED);
    }
    if (power && !stat_op_enabled && state != ST_DISABLED && state != ST_ERROR_STOP) {
        to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_DRIVE_LEFT_OPERATION_ENABLED);
    }
    /* MC_Power: Disabled -> Standstill once Enable and Status (P1 state
     * diagram), BEFORE this period's commands are judged: a command whose edge
     * comes with the power-on runs from Standstill, as after an MC_Power called
     * first in the same scan.  Done here and not inside the Disabled case, where
     * the transition used to clear the command's refusal - the command got a
     * number and then no outcome (Busy for ever at the caller). */
    if (state == ST_DISABLED && power && cfg && stat_op_enabled && !drv_fault) {
        pos_cmd_set(pos_fb); v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0; run = RUN_NONE;
        state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
        if (cmd_err == E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS) cmd_err = 0;   /* the parameters are valid now */
    }

    /* MC_SetPosition: Standstill only (P1 state diagram), refused elsewhere */
    if (set_edge && state != ST_STANDSTILL) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;

    /* ---- per-state */
    switch (state) {
    case ST_DISABLED:
        pos_cmd_set(pos_fb); v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0; run = RUN_NONE;
        if (!cfg && power) cmd_err = E_INVALID_LIMITS_OR_PARAMETERS;
        if (ex_edge || halt_edge || home_edge) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        break;

    case ST_STANDSTILL:
        v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0; run = RUN_NONE;
        if (stop_edge) {
            state_set(ST_STOPPING); run = RUN_STOP; ramps_max(__comp_inst);
            busy_set(1); active_set(1);   /* MC_Stop is Busy until standstill */
            if (drive_profile) run = RUN_NONE;   /* the drive stands: nothing to stop */
        } else if (home_edge) {
            state_set(ST_HOMING); busy_set(1); active_set(1);
            /* arm BEFORE raising the request: a model drive ties drive-home to
             * stat-homed on one signal, and the read would see our own 1 */
            home_started = !stat_homed; drive_home_set(1);
        } else if (halt_edge) {
            done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(command_id);
        } else if (set_edge) {
            /* the axis frame moves, the drive's does not: pos-cmd/pos-fb untouched */
            off = mode == 1 ? off + position : position - pos_fb;
            done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(command_id);
        } else if (ex_edge) {
            if (accept_move(__comp_inst)) { busy_set(1); active_set(1); }
        } else if (sync_edge && !drive_profile) {
            state_set(ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION);
        }
        break;

    case ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION:
        if (stop_edge) {
            busy_set(1); active_set(1);
            state_set(ST_STOPPING); run = RUN_STOP; ramps_max(__comp_inst);
        } else if (ex_edge || halt_edge || home_edge || set_edge) {
            cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        }
        if (state != ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION) break;
        if (!sync_enable) {   /* the master let go: decelerate from the last step's velocity */
            run = RUN_STOP; ramps_max(__comp_inst); state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION);
            break;
        }
        {
            double t = sync_pos - off, lo = min_limit - off, hi = max_limit - off;
            if (limits_enable && (t < lo || t > hi)) to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_SOFT_LIMIT);
            else if (fabs(t - pos_cmd) > maxv * dt) to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_SYNC_STEP_OVER_MAXV);
            else { v = (t - pos_cmd) / dt; a_cur = 0.0; pos_cmd_set(t); }
        }
        break;

    case ST_HOMING:
        /* the drive homes itself; the command follows the feedback so that no
         * following error builds up and no step is commanded on return */
        pos_cmd_set(pos_fb); v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0;
        if (ex_edge || halt_edge) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        if (stop_edge) {
            drive_home_set(0);
            end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
            busy_set(1); active_set(1);
            state_set(ST_STOPPING); run = RUN_STOP; ramps_max(__comp_inst);
        } else if (home_started && ((drv_statusword >> 13) & 1)) {
            drive_home_set(0);
            to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_HOMING_ERROR);
        } else if (!stat_homed) {
            home_started = 1;
        } else if (home_started) {
            drive_home_set(0);
            off = 0.0;   /* after homing the drive's home is the axis zero */
            complete(__comp_inst);
            state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
        }
        break;

    case ST_DISCRETE_MOTION:
    case ST_CONTINUOUS_MOTION:
        if (drive_profile) {
            /* the drive runs the profile; the axis follows its handshake */
            if (stop_edge) {
                end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
                busy_set(1); active_set(1);
                state_set(ST_STOPPING); run = RUN_STOP;
                move_acceleration_set(maxa); move_halt_set(1);
                break;
            } else if (ex_edge) {
                end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
                command_aborted_set(0);
                if (accept_move(__comp_inst)) { busy_set(1); active_set(1); }
                else { run = RUN_STOP; move_halt_set(1); state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION); }
            } else if (halt_edge) {
                end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
                busy_set(1); active_set(1);
                run = RUN_STOP; move_halt_set(1); state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION);
            } else if (home_edge) {
                cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
            }
            if (!drv_move_done) {
                move_armed = 1;
            } else if (move_armed) {
                if (run == RUN_STOP) pos_cmd_set(pos_fb);   /* halted short of the target */
                move_halt_set(0);
                complete(__comp_inst);
                run = RUN_NONE;
                state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
            }
            break;
        }
        if (stop_edge) {
            end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
            busy_set(1); active_set(1);
            state_set(ST_STOPPING); run = RUN_STOP; ramps_max(__comp_inst);
        } else if (ex_edge) {
            /* mcAborting: the new move replaces the running one from the
             * current position and velocity */
            end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
            command_aborted_set(0);
            if (accept_move(__comp_inst)) { busy_set(1); active_set(1); }
            else { run = RUN_STOP; state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION); }   /* refused: Error, not Busy */
        } else if (halt_edge) {
            /* MC_Halt: decelerate with the move's deceleration (and jerk);
             * the state is DiscreteMotion until standstill */
            end_command(__comp_inst, 1);
            busy_set(1); active_set(1);
            run = RUN_STOP; state_set(ST_DISCRETE_MOTION);
        } else if (home_edge) {
            cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        }
        if (state == ST_STOPPING) break;
        if (run == RUN_VEL && limits_enable) {
            /* a velocity move plans toward the soft limit it heads to; arriving
             * there is a soft-limit error, the profile has already stopped */
            double d = tgt - pos_cmd, stopd = v * v / (2.0 * cmd_dec);
            if ((v > 0 && d <= stopd) || (v < 0 && -d <= stopd)) { run = RUN_POS; cmd_jerk = 0.0; }
        }
        if (profile_step(__comp_inst, dt) || (run == RUN_POS && v == 0.0 && pos_cmd == tgt)) {
            if (state == ST_CONTINUOUS_MOTION && run == RUN_POS) {
                to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_SOFT_LIMIT);
                v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0; run = RUN_NONE;
            } else {
                complete(__comp_inst);
                run = RUN_NONE;
                state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
            }
        }
        break;

    case ST_STOPPING:
        if (ex_edge || halt_edge || home_edge) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        if (drive_profile) {
            if (!drv_move_done) move_armed = 1;
            else if (move_armed && run == RUN_STOP) { run = RUN_NONE; pos_cmd_set(pos_fb); }
            /* MC_Stop: Done at standstill while stop is held, Standstill on release */
            if (run == RUN_NONE && busy) complete(__comp_inst);
            if (run == RUN_NONE && !stop) {
                move_halt_set(0);
                state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
            }
            break;
        }
        if (run == RUN_STOP && profile_step(__comp_inst, dt)) run = RUN_NONE;
        /* MC_Stop: Done at standstill while stop is held (the state stays
         * Stopping), Standstill on release (P1 MC_Stop) */
        if (run == RUN_NONE && busy) complete(__comp_inst);
        if (run == RUN_NONE && !stop) state_set(ST_STANDSTILL);
        break;

    case ST_ERROR_STOP:
        if (ex_edge || halt_edge || home_edge) cmd_err = E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE;
        drive_home_set(0);
        if (!power || !stat_op_enabled) {
            /* nothing to decelerate: the drive is off, follow it */
            pos_cmd_set(pos_fb); v = 0.0; a_cur = 0.0; run = RUN_NONE;
        } else if (run == RUN_STOP && profile_step(__comp_inst, dt)) {
            run = RUN_NONE;
        }
        if (reset_edge) reset_req = 1;
        if (!reset) reset_req = reset_req && drv_fault ? 0 : reset_req;
        if (reset_req && !drv_fault && v == 0.0) {
            reset_req = 0;
            err_latched = 0;
            run = RUN_NONE;
            pos_cmd_set(pos_fb);   /* resync: MC_Reset starts from the actual position */
            if (drive_profile) move_halt_set(0);
            state_set((power && cfg && stat_op_enabled) ? ST_STANDSTILL : ST_DISABLED);
            /* MC_Reset has a Done output (PLCopen Part 1): raise it the same
             * way motion completion does, cleared on the next Execute */
            done_set(1); term_shown = 0; done_id_set(command_id);
        }
        break;

    default:  /* every state has its case; anything else is a bug */
        to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE);
        break;
    }

    fault_reset_out_set((state == ST_ERROR_STOP) && reset_req);
    vel_cmd_set(v);

    /* ---- following error: always on while the drive is powered */
    ferror_set(pos_cmd - pos_fb);
    if (!drive_profile   /* drive-profile: pos-cmd is the target, the drive's 0x6065 guards */
        && state != ST_DISABLED && state != ST_ERROR_STOP && state != ST_HOMING
        && stat_op_enabled && fabs(ferror) > ferror_max) {
        to_errorstop(__comp_inst, E_FOLLOWING_ERROR_OVER_LIMIT);
    }

    /* PLCopen Part 1, 2.4.1: Busy, Done, Error, CommandAborted exclusive in every period.
     * The newest outcome owns the outputs (see ONE MULTIPLEXED FB above). */
    error_set((err_latched != 0) || (cmd_err != 0));
    if (error) { busy_set(0); active_set(0); done_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); }
    else if (busy || done) command_aborted_set(0);
    if (busy) done_set(0);
    error_id_set(cmd_err ? cmd_err : err_latched);
    /* a command that just started running is tracked by its number; a refusal
     * of this period's command resolves it as failed */
    if (busy && !run_id) run_id = command_id;
    if (cmd_err && (ex_edge || halt_edge || stop_edge || home_edge || reset_edge || set_edge)) failed_id_set(command_id);
    axis_error_id_set(err_latched);

    actual_position_set(pos_fb + off);
    torque_fb_set((double)drv_torque);
    velocity_fb_set(drv_velocity);
    statusword_set(drv_statusword);
}
